  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&apos; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Viet Nam General Confederation of Labour (VGCL) has developed and submitted position papers on labour code revision, ratification of ILO Conventions Nos. 98 and 105, promotion of compliance with international labour standards (ILS), and on revision of the trade union law. These positions contributed to fundamental changes in the Labour code 2019. The code is now more in line with ILS, including improvement of the legal framework for employment relations, working conditions, voluntary collective negotiations (including Multi-Employers Collective Bargaining Agreement - MECBA). Most importantly, workers in enterprises can now form or join a representative organization of their own choosing. Additionally, for the application of the ILS, the Viet Nam Confederation of Labour (VGCL) has developed and issued an action plan for the implementation of Convention No. 98, which was ratified by Viet Nam in 2019. 
2. Five MECBA were signed in 2021, covering 62 enterprises, bringing benefits to 32,000 workers (48 per cent are women). Multi-employer unions were established for 10 private childcare groups with 39 kindergarten teachers in Tam Ky city, Quang Nam province. In January 2020, a trade union was established for 140 tourist boat drivers in Hoi An, Quang Nam. At the Congress, 123 Grassroots Trade Union were present and union officials (52 of which were women) were successfully elected by the workers.
3. A global labour platform/network was also established between VGCL and the European Trade Union Confederation (ETUC) to strengthen trade union capacities to monitor the implementation of EVFTA at national and global level as well as participation in Domestic Advisory Group (DAG) to better protect workers&apos; interests. The network will also act as a venue for labour solidarity and international trade union actions around the issue of trade and provide inputs and advice on the social and economic aspects of trade agreements; sharing information about labour practices of MNEs. - ILO provided technical support for Viet  Nam General Confederation of Labour (VGCL) to develop and submit their position papers on Labour Code revision, ratification of the ILO Core conventions 98, convention 105, promotion for ILS compliance, including when revising Trade Union law;
- ILO provided financial and technical support for 5 MECBAs signed among 62 enterprises bring benefits to 32,000 workers (48% are women); Multiemployer union established for 10 private childcare groups with 39 kindergarten teachers in Tam Ky city, Quang Nam province; Syndicate for 140 tourist boat drivers in Hoi An, Quang Nam established on January 2020; The democratic election promoted at 124 grass-root unions in which 123 Grassroots Trade Union  president (52 women) successfully elected by the workers at the Congress
- ILO provided financial and technical support for organizing Trade Union technical forum on the minimum wage setting and adjustment for the year of 2022, in the context of Covid-19;
- - For the promotion of the Trade Union role and participation in the UN reform, ILO  provide their technical and financial support to translate the UNSDCF guideline into Vietnamese as well as having plan to organize the national stakeholder workshop for the dissemination of this manual as well as adapting it in Viet Nam context;
-With the support of  ILO,  VGCL submitted a proposal for strengthening VGCL strategies to deal with the impact of the Free Trade Agreement through the establishment of a union network.</narrative>
   </description>
